# Runtime data
.app_data.json
.app_data.lock
daily_check.log
# Rewritten every time the server is restarted, and it holds PIDs and local
# socket state that mean nothing outside this machine. It was tracked, so every
# restart left a modification sitting in `git status` -- untracked with
# `git rm --cached`, which leaves the file on disk. Not covered by the parent
# repo's *.log rule, since it is a .txt.
restart_log.txt
hostinfo.txt
email_config.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Node
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Test output
test_reports/
test-results/
.playwright-mcp/

# Playwright screenshots from the run-canvas-app skill. Regenerated on every
# run, one set per app tested, and they had grown to 53 untracked files and
# 10.8MB -- enough to bury real work in `git status`, which is how three
# finished apps sat uncommitted for 19 days. The drivers/ beside them stay
# tracked: those are hand-written source. The few screenshots already
# committed here and under run-appverse/ predate this rule and stay, since
# ignoring a path never untracks what is already in.
.claude/skills/run-canvas-app/screenshots/

# Scheduler runtime output. The Routines/ prompts and the scripts are real
# source and stay tracked -- only what the tasks EMIT is ignored. (*.log is
# already covered by the parent .gitignore; the .out.txt twins are not.)
_scheduler/Logs/

# One-off undo manifest from the dj_music_apps cleanup; machine-specific state,
# regenerated on demand, meaningless to anyone cloning this.
_dj_cleanup_undo_manifest.json

# App content folders (both lowercase symlink-style and capitalized display names)
# action_games/* rather than action_games/ so single games can be published: git can't
# re-include a file inside an ignored directory. Ricochet Arena is on the public Arcade.
action_games/*
!action_games/2026-10-10-combat-ricochet-arena.html
adult_puzzle_apps/
art_apps/
card_games_apps/
classroom_tools/
content_creation_apps/
cooking_games/
crafts/
custom_apps/
data_visualization_apps/
dj_music_apps/
educational_apps/
fashion_apps/
health_productivity_apps/
inspirational/
music_apps/
music_game_apps/
music_production/
shooting_games_apps/
sports_games_apps/
table_games_apps/
therapy_apps/
test_apps/

# Capitalized display-name variants of the same folders
Art Apps/
Content Creation Apps/
Cooking Games/
Crafts/
Educational Apps/
Inspirational/
Kids Apps/
Music Apps/
Music Production/
Shooting Games/

# Reviews folder
Reviews/

# Generated: the concept registry is rebuilt before every routine run
# (_scheduler/Rebuild-Registry.ps1), so tracking it would dirty the tree
# ~19 times a day. Derived entirely from the apps' <!-- CONCEPT: --> headers.
_scheduler/Registry/

# Safety copies made before bulk prompt edits
_scheduler/Routines.bak-*/
_scheduler/*.bak-*

# Generated: the dashboard page rebuilds deterministically from the registry
# every time Refresh-FactoryFloor.ps1 runs. The BUILD scripts are tracked; the
# output is not, or every refresh would show up as a diff.
_scheduler/dashboard/factory.json
_scheduler/dashboard/app-factory-floor.html

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Startup launchers taken out of service; kept locally so they can be restored.
_retired_launchers/
# Scratch from QA rounds: every Playwright driver, screenshot folder, log and
# probe a review writes is named .tmp-<app>-<what>. By 16 Oct 2026 they were
# ~1,400 of the 1,477 untracked paths -- the same burying-real-work problem as
# the run-canvas-app screenshots above. Nothing named .tmp-* is source.
.tmp-*
# One-off screenshots dropped at the top level or in test_screens/ during checks.
/tablet-check.png
/test_screens/
# dj_music_apps cleanup state from Sep 2026 (quarantine copy + undo manifests),
# and the alert file the daily pollution check rewrites. Machine-local, like
# _dj_cleanup_undo_manifest.json above.
_dj_pollution_quarantine_*/
_dj_pollution_undo_*.json
dj_pollution_ALERT.txt
